# {{.Project.Name}}

A Go web service generated by [gobento](https://github.com/Tales-of-zuna/gobento).

## Run

```sh
go run ./{{.Slots.entry.Dir}}
```

The server listens on port 8080 and stores its data in `{{.Project.Name}}.db`.
Set `PORT` and `DATABASE_URL` to change them.

```sh
curl localhost:8080/health
curl -X POST localhost:8080/items -d '{"name":"first"}'
curl localhost:8080/items
```

## Test

```sh
go test ./...
```

## Layout

The code is organized by feature (a vertical slice) rather than by layer:
everything about items lives under `{{.Slots.models.Dir}}`, and code that every
feature shares lives under `internal/platform`.

| Directory | Contents |
|---|---|
| `{{.Slots.entry.Dir}}` | Entry point: configuration and wiring |
| `{{.Slots.models.Dir}}` | The items feature: the `Item` type and the `ItemStore` interface |
| `{{.Slots.handlers.Dir}}` | The feature's HTTP handlers, plus the router and `/health` |
| `{{.Slots.store.Dir}}` | The feature's data access, implementing `ItemStore` |
| `{{.Slots.database.Dir}}` | Database connection and schema, shared by all features |

Dependencies point inward: `{{.Slots.handlers.Package}}` and
`{{.Slots.store.Package}}` import `{{.Slots.models.Package}}`, never each
other, and `{{.Slots.models.Package}}` imports neither. Only
`{{.Slots.entry.Dir}}` knows every package and connects them.

### Adding a feature

To add, for example, orders next to items:

1. Create `internal/orders` with the `Order` type and an `OrderStore`
   interface.
2. Add `internal/orders/ordershttp` with its handlers and
   `internal/orders/ordersstore` implementing `OrderStore`, following the
   items packages. Add its tables to the schema in
   `{{.Slots.database.Dir}}`.
3. In `{{.Slots.entry.Dir}}/main.go`, create the store and combine the
   routers, for example with an `http.ServeMux` that sends `/orders` to the
   orders handlers and every other path to the items handlers.

A feature never imports another feature's subpackages. If orders need items,
depend on the `{{.Slots.models.Package}}` package and its interfaces.
